 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "`TesselClient` (`src/tessel/testing.py:109`) extends `werkzeug.test.Client` with these additions:\n\n- **Context preservation in a `with` block:**\n  - `__enter__` sets `preserve_context`, so the request context stays pushed after a request. You can inspect `request`, `session` and `g` afterwards.\n  - `__exit__` closes the preserved contexts.\n  - Nesting `with` blocks raises `RuntimeError`.\n  - Each new `open()` pops the previously preserved contexts, so they don't leak across redirects or repeated requests.\n- **`session_transaction()`:**\n  - It is a context manager that opens the session through a temporary test request context and yields it for modification.\n  - On exit it persists the session back into the client's cookies.\n  - It needs cookies enabled, otherwise it raises `TypeError`.\n- **Default WSGI environ:**\n  - `environ_base` is preset with `REMOTE_ADDR=127.0.0.1` and `HTTP_USER_AGENT=Werkzeug/<version>`.\n  - It is merged into every request.\n- **App-aware `open()`:**\n  - Requests are built with an `EnvironBuilder` bound to the app, so the base URL and similar settings come from the app config.\n  - It accepts an `EnvironBuilder`, an environ dict or a request object.\n  - It sets `response.json_module` to the app's `json` provider, so `response.json` uses the app's JSON handling.",
